#
# The spatial updates (ey, ex, hz) are row-major and already have good
# cache locality (j is innermost). The iterations over different rows (i)
# are independent within a fixed time step, so we can safely parallelize
# those i-loops. Exo's `parallelize_loop` primitive will lower them to
# OpenMP `#pragma omp parallel for` directives in the generated C. When
# compiled without OpenMP, these pragmas are ignored by GCC, preserving
# correctness while allowing easy tuning on multi-core systems.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

